  "releaseNotes": "Weaving strong-named assemblies is supported on all platforms.\n\nThe 'SigourneyPublishMode' property is deprecated. Weaver authors have to follow official guidance at https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/msbuild/tutorial-custom-task-code-generation on how to package an MSBuild task.\n\nThe 'SigourneyRegisteredTargetFiles' property is deprecated. Weaver authors should rename their target files to just 'MyPackage.targets' and let MSBuild automatically import them.\n\nThe 'AssemblyReference.IsReferenceAssembly' property is deprecated. All assemblies passed in WeaverConfig.References should be presumed to be reference assemblies.",
